Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T17:35:56-07:00","id":1205023,"title":"","content":"Been concocting a bunch of Japanese kiths in the background. Might be a bit before I could share any of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T18:28:43-07:00","id":1205036,"title":"","content":"I actually used the kith creation guidelines in C20 to write the wichtel and wolpertinger write-ups in C20. I\u2019ve used it for a write-up of the Dragon Kin from the Arcadia CCG I posted on the forum. I need to revisit that one and do write-ups of a few of the other Arcadia kiths sometime.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also using it as a starting point for... um, other things \ud83d\ude09","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T18:39:05-07:00","id":1205039,"title":"","content":"Was going to make my own Giant kith, until I found out that the Jotuns are apparently the Norse version of Fomorians. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Their concept would have been focused on the creation of geographical formations and natural wonders. The Seelie would have been builders and shapers, while the Unseelie would have been focused more towards destruction and cataclysmic events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-09-2018, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T18:56:02-07:00","id":1205043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1205039#post1205039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was going to make my own Giant kith, until I found out that the Jotuns are apparently the Norse version of Fomorians. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Their concept would have been focused on the creation of geographical formations and natural wonders. The Seelie would have been builders and shapers, while the Unseelie would have been focused more towards destruction and cataclysmic events.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may interject, throw canon out of the window and do it!<br /> <br /> That's a really sweet concept and would love to see (and hopefully use) the end product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T20:51:58-07:00","id":1205078,"title":"","content":"Oh man I have a lot of ideas! Oni first as a Troll Kith Subtype, but now that Hsien are Gallain they may fit there instead.<br /> <br /> Kerberoi and Barghests as Black Dog Kith/Thallain that deal with the Dead and Doomed.<br /> <br /> Imps as clever fiendish contract makers, but maybe they are instead Thallain with some sort of angel type as a kith like Grigori.<br /> <br /> Souls Tithed to Hell, a Thallain one for the damned, and a kithain version for those acting as the bounty hunters for the devil, like ghost rider. Forgot what I called them off the top of my head, maybe Furies.<br /> <br /> Doppelgangers/Fetch, as Thallain/kith who mimic mortals, maybe like Mirrorskins.<br /> <br /> Valkyrie/Dissir shieldmaiden choosers of the slain and doomed Kith/Thallain. And I think a few others that I can't remember right now. Totally using the Drakes as kith and Wyrm as Thallain though.<br /> <br /> Possibly may add Wendigo as a Thallain of the Nunnehi. A few ideas for similar ones for South America like the many trickster shapeshifter monsters with twisted legs I noticed popping up in tales.<br /> <br /> I'm a fan of possibly using Ifrit, Marid, and Djinn as Kiths, with Ghul and Iblisi/Shaitani as Thallain Genies but I feel that Genies would be their own group of Gallain like the Hsien.<br /> <br /> Minotaur and Baphomet are the Thallain I have for the Satyrs instead of the Nasties.<br /> <br /> And maybe something Cthulhu esque for more Thallain like a Cthonic kith for tentacled void dwellers under the sea/stars/earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T20:55:26-07:00","id":1205079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1205039#post1205039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was going to make my own Giant kith, until I found out that the Jotuns are apparently the Norse version of Fomorians. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Their concept would have been focused on the creation of geographical formations and natural wonders. The Seelie would have been builders and shapers, while the Unseelie would have been focused more towards destruction and cataclysmic events.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah it didn't stop canon from having Trolls, or other fan groups from detailing Fomorian courts.<br /> <br /> If I may suggest Ettins and Gigantes as Kith names if you want to have them separate from the Jotun. They could even still be descended from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T21:09:37-07:00","id":1205083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1205078#post1205078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh man I have a lot of ideas! Oni first as a Troll Kith Subtype, but now that Hsien are Gallain they may fit there instead.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I was also considering my own version of Oni as part of the Hsien. The mythology surrounding them would have even fit in theme with the rest of them. Since Oni were originally depicted as malicious spirits and later became recognized as protective guardians with defined forms.<br /> <br /> My explanation is that their original version was the Oni pretty much falling to corruption like many of the other Hsien, and after they were kicked out of heaven, they became protectors in order to atone for their previous actions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And due to their similar features, there would have been debate among the Kithain over whether or not the Oni were some oriental cousins to Trolls or Ogres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T22:41:04-07:00","id":1205100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1205036#post1205036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually used the kith creation guidelines in C20 to write the wichtel and wolpertinger write-ups in C20. I\u2019ve used it for a write-up of the Dragon Kin from the Arcadia CCG I posted on the forum. I need to revisit that one and do write-ups of a few of the other Arcadia kiths sometime.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also using it as a starting point for... um, other things \ud83d\ude09</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon Kith showing up in C20 players guide!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T05:20:06-07:00","id":1205146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1205100#post1205100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon Kith showing up in C20 players guide!</div> </div> </div> </div>HA! If one does, it won\u2019t be by me \ud83d\ude01","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T13:10:33-07:00","id":1205347,"title":"","content":"I'm working on building a kitsune kith for an NPC in my game. It's been interesting so far but I'm having a hard time getting anything concrete written down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24109-calder","name":"Calder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T15:58:27-07:00","id":1205407,"title":"","content":"I've been wanting to add Norse style Dwarves, but I'm not sure how to make them work without coming off as &quot;better Nockers&quot; same with Cyclopses, by giving them a different frailty but making them expert crafters it kind hits at &quot;why go to the Nockers they just fuck things up&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 04-10-2018, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T01:08:22-07:00","id":1205490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1205407#post1205407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been wanting to add Norse style Dwarves, but I'm not sure how to make them work without coming off as &amp;quot;better Nockers&amp;quot; same with Cyclopses, by giving them a different frailty but making them expert crafters it kind hits at &amp;quot;why go to the Nockers they just fuck things up&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In both cases the price of doing business would be the point. Both the Norse Dwarves and the Cyclopses were sinister and dangerous creatures. I'd make them Thallain or close to it. You can live with a Nocker's price. Underline the word live. The other two were icehearted killers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T04:57:04-07:00","id":1205536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1205490#post1205490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In both cases the price of doing business would be the point. Both the Norse Dwarves and the Cyclopses were sinister and dangerous creatures. I'd make them Thallain or close to it. You can live with a Nocker's price. Underline the word live. The other two were icehearted killers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nockers are sinister and dangerous creatures.. that cut corners then. I mean they still come off as the &quot;cheap knock off&quot; version even if their price is too much.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the cyclops situation I was rereading the various bits of Greek myth and while there are bits where they are actual crafters they are more famous crafters as assistants to Hephaestus and I think I have the dividing point better figured out. Cyclopses are kind of lazy thinkers. If you want a guy who can litterally punch steel until you have a fine sword you go to a cyclops, it won't be pretty, it won't have any unique features but it will be well balanced and sharp. You go to a Nocker to get a puzzle sword! But as assistants Cyclopses well they make everyone better, you have a Nocker or a Dougal Lord with a Cyclops right hand man? People mistake a master craftsman for Hephaestus himself!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T11:21:11-07:00","id":1206095,"title":"","content":"Thing is Boggans and Knockers were made to fill in multiple types of creatures, everything from Brownies,Dwarger, Svartalfar, Domovoi and Cobolds. But after the core kiths were made they took a 180 and instead of kiths being broad archetypes the new kiths were specific examples. So now what we would make Boggans more Brownies specifically and Dwarves something else?<br /> <br /> You could also use the old Boggan Birthright and make it that Dwarves have a lowered difficulty for crafting. I would make the Cyclops Thaillain if not outright Fomorians though.<br /> <br /> Why not start making Fomorians, they are foes and gotta fight them some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T18:19:41-07:00","id":1206212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1206095#post1206095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is Boggans and Knockers were made to fill in multiple types of creatures, everything from Brownies,Dwarger, Svartalfar, Domovoi and Cobolds. But after the core kiths were made they took a 180 and instead of kiths being broad archetypes the new kiths were specific examples. So now what we would make Boggans more Brownies specifically and Dwarves something else?<br /> <br /> You could also use the old Boggan Birthright and make it that Dwarves have a lowered difficulty for crafting. I would make the Cyclops Thaillain if not outright Fomorians though.<br /> <br /> Why not start making Fomorians, they are foes and gotta fight them some time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel Boggans decently cover house fairies, but feel Nocker Frailty very much pushes it towards the mad genius, which is neat but means sort of related crafter types end up some place else. Similarly I think there's a solid &quot;Angry violent big guy&quot; archtype that Trolls don't quite cover with their whole super honorable thing, thus why when people say &quot;just use trolls for oni&quot; I don't think it works... conversely if Oni had been the generic kith I'd argue they better cover a wide variety of Big angry type giants including Rock giants from the Nunnehi.<br /> <br /> Thus why I a troll crafter with one Eye wouldn't hit my &quot;I want to play a cyclops&quot; vibe. Thus why Nockers don't hit my &quot;I want to play a dwarf&quot;(who are mentioned in the troll book btw..).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T21:57:56-07:00","id":1206275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1206212#post1206212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I feel Boggans decently cover house fairies, but feel Nocker Frailty very much pushes it towards the mad genius, which is neat but means sort of related crafter types end up some place else. Similarly I think there's a solid &quot;Angry violent big guy&quot; archtype that Trolls don't quite cover with their whole super honorable thing, thus why when people say &quot;just use trolls for oni&quot; I don't think it works... conversely if Oni had been the generic kith I'd argue they better cover a wide variety of Big angry type giants including Rock giants from the Nunnehi.<br /> <br /> Thus why I a troll crafter with one Eye wouldn't hit my &quot;I want to play a cyclops&quot; vibe. Thus why Nockers don't hit my &quot;I want to play a dwarf&quot;(who are mentioned in the troll book btw..).</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhh but they made a type of Honor Troll just for the game, so why would Oni be better, they could have just made Trolls like mythic Trolls.<br /> <br /> And if I were to make Oni Trolls they would be a SubKith, so they wouldn't use the same exact rules, they would have other ones. But Buddhist Oni could actually fit the Honor thing since they often made promises that tied their wellness and strength too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T22:22:37-07:00","id":1206285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1206275#post1206275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uhh but they made a type of Honor Troll just for the game, so why would Oni be better, they could have just made Trolls like mythic Trolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could have. I'm saying if they had a generic Oni kith of strong angry guy, I'd be more than willing to say &quot;use that for Trolls/giants/etc&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if I were to make Oni Trolls they would be a SubKith, so they wouldn't use the same exact rules, they would have other ones. But Buddhist Oni could actually fit the Honor thing since they often made promises that tied their wellness and strength too. </div> </div> </div>I don't think the honor thing empowering them actually works for oni at all? It is because Oaths are so hard and painful that make them so important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T16:54:06-07:00","id":1207062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1205078#post1205078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a fan of possibly using Ifrit, Marid, and Djinn as Kiths, with Ghul and Iblisi/Shaitani as Thallain Genies but I feel that Genies would be their own group of Gallain like the Hsien.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. It seems from my readings in modern Arab folklore, limited as those are, that the jinni are divided into tribes designated by color. I'd treat this somewhat like the noble houses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T21:09:49-07:00","id":1207147,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s an intestine idea. I was originally thinking of Iblis as a Thallain house and all the others as Kiths but this is interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T21:21:01-07:00","id":1207150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1207147#post1207147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s an intestine idea. I was originally thinking of Iblis as a Thallain house and all the others as Kiths but this is interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps, some jinn are held to be pagans. Others are Muslim, some are said to be Christian or Jewish. None are necessarily bad or good. Most are dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T14:08:08-07:00","id":1208169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths#post1204987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the title says, has anyone taken the option of making their own kith? If so tell us about it.<br /> <br /> Later on, when I've checked my notes, I'll describe the one off Changeling, who was a kith of one, I created.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I prefer DA Fae to CtD. Faeries are so varied that a free-form creation system is so much better","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T16:50:12-07:00","id":1208238,"title":"","content":"I posted a homebrew Kith some time ago, in a thread to that effect: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092218-post-your-homebrew-kiths\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...homebrew-kiths</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T16:56:44-07:00","id":1208244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1208169#post1208169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I prefer DA Fae to CtD. Faeries are so varied that a free-form creation system is so much better</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've found a full freeform system has its issues as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T00:30:14-07:00","id":1211711,"title":"","content":"So the Electric Shadow Kith I am making for the Yokai project are a cluster of kiths. Basically they are Changelings that were Unnamed and eventually were reborn merging with Chimera of the Cinema. Making Subkiths like Cowboy, Samurai, Beauty, Buffoon, Martial Artist, Swashbuckler, ect. They number in the handful, some maybe even the only member of the subkith. Till the Evanescence and their numbers bolster by a few dozen.<br /> <br /> Then there was also the older Idea I had of Witches as a Kith with birthrights of maybe using sympathetic links to use arts on subjects, and or a Familiar. Their Thallain could be a Warlock representing one who sold themselves to dark powers for might.<br /> <br /> Also more on the Gargoyle Project.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1207483-lets-discuss-making-a-gargoyle-kith#post1207483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one of the ideas I had, and I remember a few others brought up, was creating a Kith similar to the Gargoyles from the old disney cartoon. So the idea would be Fae, lets say some Inanimae so the Dreams/Myths of the very Elements chose to take refuge in the Flesh. So they are like a mix of the Inanimae , in their primal inhuman dreams, and the Merfolk, who took refuge in the flesh but breed within their own communities living away from humanity.<br /> <br /> So the Gargoyles are born from Eggs that come from Gargoyle pairs, or human/Gargoyle pairings. They are raised in private groups, and to help shield from Banality they turn to stone the moment the Sun Rises and return to flesh by night.<br /> <br /> They would say perhaps have Houses for different types of statues, or possibly different Kiths.<br /> <br /> House F<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u00f3sh\u012b</span></span></span>: For Fu Lions and Fu Dogs, and Sacred Guardian Beasts like Dragons and Directional Beasts. Homeland originated in East Asia.<br /> <br /> House Shedu: For Guardians of Necropoli , and plumbers of Underworld lore. They Originated in Egypt, but also include the Sumerian Bearded Lion/Bull iconography.<br /> <br /> House Babewyn: The standard Gargoyles, Grotesques and Chimera statues popularly found in Cathedrals, originated in France and spread the quickest and farthest of all the Houses. Guardians of the cities and highest points.<br /> <br /> House <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u015aakra: Those gargoyles invoking demonic guardians like Asura, and Animal headed and horned guardians of hell, originating in Buddhist Territories ranging from Indian, Tibet, and Japan.<br /> <br /> House Binesi: Gargoyles invoking the Totempole Iconography, these Gargoyles actually turn into Wood during the day and take the form of Clan Totem animals and even the Thunderbird. They are a house of Teachers.<br /> <br /> House Kisin: Statues of Death and Skeletons originating in the Americas, the represent Gods such as Mictlantecuhtli and skeletal motiffs . They embrace cannibalism, death and rebirth.<br /> <br /> Maybe though they call their Houses Clans, invoking the Doodem of the Ojibwe.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> So maybe include Birthrights for Flying, and a physical Boost. Maybe for nonhumanoid shapes they can switch between humanoid and beast form.<br /> <br /> What are some thoughts and ideas for these Gallain ? I'm thinking they heal all bashing Damage and one Lethal while in stone slumber. Maybe they also convert one agg to Lethal too.<br /> <br /> They would also have Fae beasts, similar to how Gargoyles had Bronx and Boudicca?<br /> <br /> I think this would be most fun in the Changeling setting rather then their own thing, but they would likely touch upon Wraith and the Fera as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1209960-y\u014dkai-and-gallain-shifting-to-other-gallain-kithain-groups\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...kithain-groups</a>And the link to the Yokai one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T11:00:00-07:00","id":1211894,"title":"","content":"Electric shadows- Have you considered making them Inanimae instead? the Flicker Empire hasn't gotten much development and it sounds like it would be hitting on similar ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> Witch-quick thoughts.<br /> <br /> Affinity: Prop.(&quot;EAT THIS POISON APPLE!&quot;)<br /> <br /> BR:<br /> <br /> &quot;I curse you by the hairs on your head&quot;-Witches may cast arts as if touching the the target if they have hair, skin, blood that is no older than two weeks from the body.<br /> <br /> Unearthly beauty-we know how this works!<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> Something else-For the option of making a witch who is not the fairest in the land... <br /> <br /> <br /> FR:<br /> <br /> Pride: Witches are prideful creatures. Either in a pariticular aspect of their physical form(&quot;who's the fairest in the land..&quot;) or a particular skill they have, or just assume they are going to be invited to the christening of children. Suffice to say they are easily slighted. a Witch who is slighted who does not curse their victim recieves a Nightmare Dice.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T21:20:48-07:00","id":1212137,"title":"","content":"<br /> Hmm no I never considered Inanimae. So you mean like the Empire of Flickers for Inanimae of Light and Radiowaves?<br /> Hmm.<br /> <br /> Yeah I was thinking Prop too. I was thinking on the Flaw, anything from cannot harm the innocent, or other witchy flaws. Yeah that was along the lines of the Sympathetic Magic Birthright I was thinking of. So you think its too powerful without limiting the freshness of the blood sample?<br /> <br /> Another Birthright might be their Fae Soul is placed into their Familiar, and they are like a living version of the Selkie Coat. Or maybe instead of the Sympathetic magic they can cast arts through their Familiar as well as through themselves. And maybe their Familiar has stealth and nigh immortality, or maybe they are built like Chimerae but bound to a mortal animal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T21:42:20-07:00","id":1212145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1212137#post1212137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm no I never considered Inanimae. So you mean like the Empire of Flickers for Inanimae of Light and Radiowaves?<br /> Hmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are briefly mentioned afew times in the books and Nockers apparently have some idea they exist.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah I was thinking Prop too. I was thinking on the Flaw, anything from cannot harm the innocent, or other witchy flaws. </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking solidly on the theme of fairy tale witches vs &quot;ANY WITCH EVER&quot; since that's mage. Fairy tale witches are VERY good at harming the innocent especially when they are angered.<br /> <br /> Snow White and Sleeping beauty would be my primaries. Perhaps Circe.<br /> <br /> I am not sure if a separate &quot;Hag&quot; should be a thing or just their grump version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah that was along the lines of the Sympathetic Magic Birthright I was thinking of. So you think its too powerful without limiting the freshness of the blood sample? </div> </div> </div>two weeks might be too short, maybe a year and a day.. I'm spitballing. I don't like the idea of &quot;THIS LASTS FOREVER&quot; in changeling..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another Birthright might be their Fae Soul is placed into their Familiar, and they are like a living version of the Selkie Coat. Or maybe instead of the Sympathetic magic they can cast arts through their Familiar as well as through themselves. And maybe their Familiar has stealth and nigh immortality, or maybe they are built like Chimerae but bound to a mortal animal. </div> </div> </div>I can't think of a fairy tale witch that has a familiar. Superior beauty? Inhuman strength?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T00:08:01-07:00","id":1212166,"title":"","content":"Well I was thinking they were the Mage inspired kith specifically and broadly applicable. Like I have the Beasties be inspired by the Fera, and a new kith the Strigoi inspired by Vampires. The idea I got was from Baba Yaga Tales were Baba Yaga only seemed to harm people that offended her, so she couldn't get at Vassila the Pure. So its going off the Folkore Witches that used Familiars, that way they could also be used very far and wide, even among the Nunnehi and the Wandering Dream's Kith. Originally before Warlocks I was thinking of Hags as my Thallain, but I changed it partly because we already have the River Hags and Bodhach. But I feel already Unseelie Sidhe, Ailill and Eiluned particularly, fill the Role of Fairytale Fair witches and I wanted one that could fit other aspects. As already many of the Faerytale witches were royals. So I want some Baba Yaga's and Aboriginal Witches. In fact I think the Skin Walkers would already fit the Nunnehi Thallain of these fellas. Circe Again is a noble Witch, being a child of divine beings. Though I guess many of the Witches weren't impossible Beauties besides Snow Whites Mum in law and Circes for the most part being particularly hot, but not the World's hottest. And most being just somewhat attractive Enchantresses (Another Kith name I considered for them back with Enchanters being the Kith and Hags being the Thallain). So these Witches I could have fill the Roles of Baba Yaga, and the Troll Mothers of Norse tradition like Angraboda, the Giantess Voluspa, and various Italian folklore about witches selling their souls to the devil. Plus having a Familiar would be a rather unique Birthright kinda fun and different.<br /> <br /> One of the limits I considered was maybe they need the hair or blood or whatever willingly given to them. Or what about using a sample for a bunk uses up the sample in casting the cantrip.<br /> <br /> The Disney Maleficent had that Crow/Raven she had a hardon for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So Strigoi/Vrykolakas were another Kith, they could say suffer -4 pain penalties for activity in the Daylight until they can slumber in the dark of the Earth or Water for a day. Or maybe some similar penalty if they don't consume human blood, or supernatural, blood what once a week? Once every other Day? Also having to make a roll to resist consuming blood? Maybe gain enhanced healing or physicality after feeding? Maybe a glamour pool that can offset Cantrip costs that can be replenished with drinking blood? Or a ban against running water, or Running water paralyzes them? Or Holy Symbols and Garlic repel them? Though they could be the more primitive Thallain to say a Baobhan Kith of seducers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm now I just need Kiths for say Mummies and Hunters. Maybe Also Prometheans. Dauntain/Autumn People kind of already fit the Hunter Roles. Or maybe take a note from the Lost and do a Huntsmen Kith representing maybe Cernunnos and the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> Huntsmen for the Kith and I don't know what yet for a Thallain, maybe Stalkers playing off of the unseen watchers particularly proliferated in Urban Legends, like the Call Came from inside the House and what not.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Revanent Kith for Mummies, and maybe Prometheans. That keep coming back from the dead in the form of a birthright of extra coma/torpor health levels? Or some other similar effect. Maybe Zombi are Thallain that are often either simple or easily enslaved/dominated and maybe hunger for brains/flesh.<br /> <br /> Also I expect we eventually will get a Hulda, it just seems like a perfect Kith, but I guess I should bang one out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T00:41:57-07:00","id":1212168,"title":"","content":"Also maybe a Hunter Kith could be the Benandanti, yes I know Wraith uses them but I am admiting they are Kiths inspired by existent beings. they could hunt Thallain, Witches, Ghosts and Demons, probably often joining house Beaumayn. Their Thallain could be Malandanti, or Strigoi/Strega for another type of Witch, in the form of a Thallain Kith that specifically curses folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T01:30:05-07:00","id":1212176,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;Kith that is based on the dreams of another prodigal&quot; is not game space worth developing it both undercuts the &quot;Changeling story&quot; and would probably work better in a full on Lost girl &quot;There aren't prodigals' setup where everything is covered by changelings of some fashion. Second I think every urban myth gets a kith/thallain is sort of undersells the whole &quot;the dreaming is dying..&quot;<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean though I think say for example a Baba/Hag based on Baba Yaga and her kin would be bad space, just that &quot;VAMPIRE&quot; kith would be a bad one, or &quot;HUNTER&quot; kith would be a bad one. I think generally there is a certain amount of inhumanity built into what should be a fairy, a sense of the the other worldlyness, Modern kiths I'd try would be cryptids possibly aliens(one could even play up the &quot;no we've always been here..&quot; chariots of the gods stuff..)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T01:48:00-07:00","id":1212179,"title":"","content":"I original was very much against things like Kiths based on other supernaturals that already exist, like Vampire Kiths since we already have Cainites. I was eventually won over however, I remember someone else arguing the idea of Enchanters for instance being a Mage stand in Kith, and the C20 book really encouraging it. Because for one these are Kiths based on the Folklore and Myth and function well even if you don't have Prodigals, like Strigoi/Vryakokas are not really so much based on Cainites they are based on rural myths. Its kind of a meta thought exercise. The C20 book really embraces homebrewing, and these wouldn't be Kiths that have numbers that equal the numbers of say Pooka or Boggans. Before I read the Kith Creation section in C20 I wouldn't of made the Electric Shadows because they aren't Faery myths, they are movie Archetypes but the Kith Creation section talks about why not try making Kiths that aren't copy and paste myths and something new, also inspired by the spirit of creation that went into making the Fan-kith Jongaleurs. So I like the idea of lots of Kiths exist that don't really number very high, and are really nonstandard like how Selkies don't really work like normal kiths like Boggans, their Souls are linked to their Pelts and are passed on to relatives.<br /> <br /> So it isn't really a VAMPIRE Kith, but it is a Vampire Kith in the sense of Witch/Vampire/Evil spirit folklorish beings. Its vampire in the meta sense particularly of what inspires the creation of the kith as a though exercise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T01:49:58-07:00","id":1212180,"title":"","content":"And these aren't the Dreams of Prodigals. These are Dreams of Humans based off of themes influenced by Prodigals. Because as I point out I see the Beasties pretty much representing the Nightmares of the Impergium, its literally in their Birthrights and Frailty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T01:15:19-07:00","id":1212561,"title":"","content":"Einherjar could be an immortal warrior Kith, with Draugr as the Undead Thallain. Popular with House Aesin.<br /> <br /> Berserkers/Riastrad/Ulfhednar Berserker Kiths who gain strength and invulnerability from Rage at the cost of Madness. Still thinking up Thallain, maybe Grendel, but I do like Grendel as a one off.<br /> <br /> A big one I was mulling over all day was:<br /> <br /> The Chosen: Fabled Weapons of Yore have stirred into unease underneath the Red Star and they choose worthy men and women. Perhaps what starts it off is Caliburn no longer finds King David Worthy. Perhaps even during this time David dies or nearly dies only to be saved by Caliburn Ex Calibur's return from Arcadia alongside the other weapons of the Gods, in the hands of mortals now newly made into fabled heroes. The weapons themselves would be the Birthrights and they would make their chosen wielder something akin to Selkies, tying their faery soul to the weapon. So maybe a crippled doctor finds a wooden stick but upon tapping it on the ground he can see it is actually a Thunder Gods Hammer. Finding a rusted sword in a log a disinherited bastard becames a true king. Not all are weapons though, A beautiful supermodel falls from grace due to a pill addiction, and laying in a gutter in a puddle of her own shame she throws away her ill gotten gains and finds <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">Br\u00edsingamen </span></span> and walks like a Goddess.<br /> <br /> The Accursed: The Thallain counterpoints to the Chosen. These are those doomed to stumble upon cursed items, owned by wicked beings. Like the Hook of a Pirate King that hungers for Blood, the Glass Eye of Killer of a hundred men both on the battlefield and off, the knives of an infamously saucy Victorian Killer, or the Cursed Muramasa Blades and or the Sword Tyrfing. Fafnir's Ring would be a perfect example too.<br /> <br /> I was thinking again on Djinn. The explaination for why some Djinn underwent an equivalent of the Changeling Ways and some don't. Perhaps some Djinn were lost since they were very first imprisoned in a vessel and they eventually discover they can use a miracle to summon a mortal to free them but only if they merge with the Mortals. So they would be another Fae type that connects their fae Soul to an item, their old prison vessel, like a Jar, or even a jeweled ring. Perhaps the Fae/Tuatha/Fomorians taught the Djinn this Miracle to bolster their Numbers, or even Angels and Demons.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps Solomon and his peers gave an Ultimatum to a portion of the Djinn, if they agreed to incarnate into mortal bodies, they wouldn't spend an eternity imprisoned, only Millenia. Their prison sentence is up by the time of the Shattering.<br /> <br /> Or Perhaps a handful of Djinn avoid Prison Altogether by taking up the Changeling Way ritual, this would mean they took it up the Changeling Way Ritual like over two thousand years before the Kithain. Or maybe they took it up after the Shattering, because they were freed Djinn that wished to avoid Taftani Sorcerers' Enslavement and became Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T02:30:51-07:00","id":1212571,"title":"","content":"I'll have to find that book I bought on the Djinni in modern Arab folklore and tell you the name and ISBN. It even has accounts by people who claimed to speak to the djinni.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T03:12:08-07:00","id":1212577,"title":"","content":"I'll add it to my must read lists. I need to compile lists of books on Folklore of the Americas, Africa, and Australia,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T13:26:06-07:00","id":1212776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1212571#post1212571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to find that book I bought on the Djinni in modern Arab folklore and tell you the name and ISBN. It even has accounts by people who claimed to speak to the djinni.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Legends-Fire-Spirits-Genies-Zanzibar/dp/1780769040/\" target=\"_blank\">Legends of the Fire Spirits</a>, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T15:46:57-07:00","id":1212822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1212776#post1212776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.amazon.com/Legends-Fire-Spirits-Genies-Zanzibar/dp/1780769040/&amp;quot;]Legends</a> of the Fire Spirits[/URL], maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I was going nuts looking for it. My sister straightened my books out and I can't find anything. <br /> <br /> Great book isn't it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T05:12:34-07:00","id":1214111,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Alright, I've finally gotten around to writing up a basic idea of what I'm thinking of regarding a Giant kith.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">----------------------------------------------</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Giants:</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I like to travel the world every couple of reincarnations. It gives me the chance to see how well my handiwork has endured throughout the ages.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> From time immemorial, humans have always told stories of the Giants. Such creatures were often the source of awe inspiring works of creation, or cataclysmic acts of destruction. Wherever the Giants went, they left their mark on the world, marks that would often persist for centuries long after their original creators had moved on. Legends even say they were responsible for sculpting the world's land masses into what they are today. Giants represent dreams of lasting impact and historical significance. They are masters of both construction and destruction. With the Long Winter growing ever closer, many Changelings believe that the Giants are needed now more than ever, if they hope to rekindle humanity's spark of creativity.<br /> <br /> While many cultures have their own stories of Giants, the most iconic ones are perhaps members of the Nordic variety. These Kithain are said to be distantly related to Trolls in some fashion and also claim to have originally been the rulers of their own kingdom before suffering a fall from grace. It is unclear whether or not the Sidhe were responsible for their fall, as they allegedly were for the lost Troll kingdom, but the Nordic Giants still remember its name. They claim that the ruins of Jotunheim still exist within the Deep Dreaming, and if they could find a way to get back there, they would have the chance to rebuild their legacy. While this was initially considered to be a wishful fantasy, the Kithain have noticed the Giants are becoming increasingly more fixated on the legendary kingdom as the Long Winter becomes harder to ignore.<br /> <br /> Whether a Giant leans more towards creation or destruction is largely dependent upon their court. Those of the Seelie affiliation tend to favor their more creative aspects, possibly due to the fact the traditionalist houses are more likely to continue appreciating their contributions. By contrast, those of the Unseelie affiliation tend to embrace their more destructive aspects, seeking to tear the world down around them. Some among the Unseelie claim that they do this as a test, to reveal who has the strength to recover from the aftermath of a tragedy, but others are just happy to vent their frustrations upon a world that no longer believes in them.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> For the most part, Giants could pass themselves off as humans, if it weren't for their most outstanding trait, being their mythical size. Giants often tower over anything that does not have the description of 'colossal' or 'titanic' attached to it. A fully mature Giant can reach heights of 10 feet tall and weighing several hundred pounds in the Near Dreaming, while only continuing to expand in size as they travel further in! Nordic Giants often favor braiding their hair, regardless of gender and many among the male population take pride in growing full beards to accentuate their facial features.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Childling:</b> Even from a young age, Giants display an interest in creative expression. Their toy boxes often contain a variety of hobby kits and play sets which they can use to bring their imaginations to life. Members of the Seelie Court take joy in assembling creative environments and acting out the lives of the people who reside within it, while those of the Unseelie Court usually take pleasure in destroying the finished creations, often in a dramatically exaggerated fashion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wilder:</b> Upon reaching some form of maturity, many Giants feel the urge to leave their mark upon the world. What was once a simple hobby now becomes a professional career, as the Seelie begin to follow the dreams they've had since childhood. Those of the Unseelie, however, are often frustrated by exposure to a world that doesn't support their ideas or believes in their creative potential, so they begin to lash out against the system and those who they feel are being given more praise than they deserve.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Grump:</b> For the most part, Giants who have progressed into Grumps seem to have mellowed with age. Seelie Court members have left behind a legacy of accomplishments that they can look back upon and smile proudly. Some hope to complete one final project before their time is up, but most decide that it's time for them to pass their skills on to a few apprentices so that their ideas will live on in others. Unseelie Grumps, however, often become crotchety old geezers who are angry at the world for never fully appreciating their talents. Blaming their lack of success upon interference by others, these Giants aren't so much interested in fostering their apprentice's growth, but rather they view them as an opportunity to live vicariously through their accomplishments. Such lack of proper nurturing often leaves their apprentices feeling just as frustrated as their teachers, thus leading to a new generation of Unseelie destroyers as the cycle begins again.<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Birthrights:</b><br /> <br /> <i>World Builder</i> - The handiwork of a Giant will last throughout the ages, or at the very least will take hundreds of years before it starts to show signs of degradation. In exchange for a point of Glamour during a Crafts roll, the Giant reduces the difficulty by -2. Additionally, Giants can never botch a Crafts roll.<br /> <br /> <i>Might of the Jotun</i> - The title of Giant is almost synonymous with physical power. At character creation, the Giant gains a bonus of +2 to Strength, even if this would take them beyond 5. Additionally, the Giant gains a +1 to their bruised health rating. This bonus stacks with the Huge Size merit, should you wish to take it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Frailty:</b><br /> <br /> <i>Cramped Spaces</i> - Even the tiniest Giant stands on par with the tallest of humans. Giants have great difficulty fitting themselves inside of places not designed to accommodate their size. Should the Giant attempt to enter a space that is less than 10 feet high and 7 feet wide, they must spend a point of Willpower to do so, and they immediately risk triggering banality in the process. For every 2 rounds they continue to remain within the confined area, they risk an additional banality trigger, which causes many in the autumn world to assume they are claustrophobic.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-02-2018, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T05:49:41-07:00","id":1214116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1204987-have-you-made-your-own-kiths?p=1214111#post1214111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Birthrights:</b><br /> <br /> <i>World Builder</i> - The handiwork of a Giant will last throughout the ages, or at the very least will take hundreds of years before it starts to show signs of degradation. In exchange for a point of Glamour during a Crafts roll, the Giant achieves an Exceptional Success upon earning 3 or more successes, as opposed to the usual 5. Additionally, Giants can never botch a Crafts roll.<br /> <br /> <i>Might of the Jotun</i> - The title of Giant is almost synonymous with physical power. At character creation, the Giant gains a bonus of +2 to Strength, even if this would take them beyond 5. Additionally, the Giant gains a +1 bonus to their Size rating for the purpose of determining Health levels. While in the Autumn World, this size bonus only serves as an effective rating, but in the Dreaming, it can manifest as an actual increase in bodily proportions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Frailty:</b><br /> <br /> <i>Cramped Spaces</i> - Even the tiniest Giant stands on par with the tallest of humans. Giants have great difficulty fitting themselves inside of places not designed to accommodate their size. Should they attempt to do so, the Giant must spend a point of Willpower and immediately risks triggering banality. For every 2 rounds they continue to remain within the confined area, they risk an additional banality trigger, which causes many in the autumn world to assume they are claustrophobic.[/SIZE]</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm loving this i'm probably going to steal world builder for my Cyclops idea, I like the idea of Cramped spaces but could it be more specific? Is a &quot;normal&quot; house an issue? i","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-0